  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-09T02:50:44.266Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I often play Suika game (https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_15f7034a-b074-4812-bfcb-317eaa2741de) in desktop mode using a small cat avatar (https://osatoubox.booth.pm/items/4183060). Yesterday I noticed that the game controller has became huge, covering almost half of my screen. There haven't been any changes to the world itself, so I suspect this issue is related to the recent update:\n\n\"When grasping objects on a flatscreen device (desktop, mobile) the position of the avatar's hand should be consistent for avatars of different scales.\"\n\nThis change makes it difficult to play the game using small avatars, as the oversized controller obstructs the view.\n\nI've included two pictures showing the issue - before and after the change.",
